body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `canonicalJson` function treats TypedArrays (such as `Uint8Array` or `Uint32Array`) and `Buffer` instances as plain objects because `typeof item === 'object'` is true and `Array.isArray(item)` is false. This causes `Object.keys(item).sort()` to sort their numeric indices alphabetically (e.g., `'10'` before `'2'`), which shuffles and corrupts the sequence of elements when serialized. Since `operatorList.fnArray` is a TypedArray, any page with 10 or more operators will have its operators shuffled, resulting in an incorrect and non-deterministic `operatorDigest`.

To fix this, convert TypedArrays and Buffers to standard arrays before serialization.

```javascript
export function canonicalJson(value) {
  return JSON.stringify(value, (_, item) => {
    if (item && ArrayBuffer.isView(item) && !(item instanceof DataView)) {
      return Array.from(item);
    }
    return item && typeof item === 'object' && !Array.isArray(item)
      ? Object.fromEntries(Object.keys(item).sort().map(key => [key, item[key]])) : item;
  });
}
```

